{
 "what": "R_v2 detections against the p014-p020 .atr annotations; descriptive only, affects no result.",
 "method": "R_v2 detections come from the frozen code (signal_path, features.record_state) run from native counts on the whole record, exactly as in forecasting. Window 10 s <= time < 290 s for both detections (grid index 2500..72499) and annotations (native sample 50,000..1,449,999). Shares (literal, as the protocol words it): annotated beats with a detection within 50 ms (nearest detection), and detections with an annotated beat within 50 ms. Detection time is the grid endpoint k / 250 s with no delay compensation, as in the protocol's grid. Supplementary, stated before running: the same shares with detection times moved 20 ms earlier, the filter's group delay given in PROTOCOL.json section 7, and the median signed offset.",
 "annotation_channels": "Each .atr file marks every beat twice, once with WFDB chan 0 and once with chan 1. The chan field is the signal number in the header (0 = ECG lead I, 1 = ECG lead II); R_v2 runs on lead II. Shares are given per channel. A first private run of this check pooled both channels, which counts each beat twice; it is superseded by this per-channel file.",
